Teach scripts/ld-version.sh about the mold linker.

Upstream only accepts "GNU ld" (BFD) and LLD, every other linker is
rejected with "unknown linker" and the build dies before compiling.
mold prints `mold <ver> (compatible with GNU ld)` on --version, so report
it as BFD with mold's own version, this keeps CONFIG_LD_IS_BFD set and the
high version number avoids the old-binutils workarounds.

mold has no built-in LTO, it needs the LLVMgold.so plugin passed via -plugin
by a clang driver that sees -flto, the kernel links vmlinux by calling LD
directly so that never happens, therefore mold is only valid for non-LTO
builds (USE handles the lto/cfi/autofdo/propeller exclusions).

--- a/scripts/ld-version.sh
+++ b/scripts/ld-version.sh
@@ -41,6 +41,11 @@
 elif [ "$1" = GNU -a "$2" = gold ]; then
 	echo "gold linker is not supported as it is not capable of linking the kernel proper." >&2
 	exit 1
+elif [ "$1" = mold ]; then
+	version=$2
+	min_version=$($min_tool_version binutils)
+	name=BFD
+	disp_name="mold"
 else
 	while [ $# -gt 1 -a "$1" != "LLD" ]; do
 		shift
